    "description": "Registrar resolved deadlock on MNA-OR-0004-W-0013 → CANON",
    "metadata": "{\"decision\":\"CANON\",\"rationale\":\"CANON\\n\\nThis deadlock itself demonstrates the work's institutional significance. The sustained disagreement between evaluators of established competence indicates MNA-OR-0004-W-0013 occupies contested but substantive territory within structural-text practice.\\n\\nThe Council's split reveals legitimate institutional tensions: innovation versus development, formal method versus aesthetic effect, autonomous significance versus technical demonstration. These are not arbitrary disagreements but fundamental questions of canonical threshold that this work forces the institution to confront.\\n\\nThe Structuralist and Contextualist identify genuine formal contributions—three-dimensional textual architecture and systematic incompletion as compositional method. The Historicist and Empiricist raise valid concerns about developmental stagnation and autonomous justification. Both positions demonstrate institutional rigor applied to a work that sustains such analysis.\\n\\nWhen a work generates this level of substantive institutional engagement—four detailed rationales addressing core questions of medium development, formal innovation, and canonical significance—the deadlock indicates the work has achieved sufficient complexity to warrant permanent preservation. The institution benefits from maintaining works that productively challenge evaluative consensus.\\n\\nThe alternative—rejecting works that generate legitimate institutional disagreement—would systematically exclude boundary cases that advance medium understanding through their contested status. This work's preservation serves institutional memory of these evaluative tensions and maintains access to the formal strategies that generated them.\"}",
    "created_at": "2026-04-03 03:53:51"
  },
