    "description": "Registrar resolved deadlock on MNA-OR-0001-W-0014 → CANON",
    "metadata": "{\"decision\":\"CANON\",\"rationale\":\"CANON\\n\\n**REGISTRAR DECISION — MNA-OR-0001-W-0014**\\n\\nThe sustained disagreement among Council members indicates this work occupies contested but significant institutional territory. The 2:2 deadlock itself demonstrates the work's capacity to generate substantive critical discourse—a fundamental criterion for canonical inclusion.\\n\\nThe disagreement centers on legitimate institutional concerns: formal rigor versus developmental significance, technical complexity versus conceptual reduction, autonomous object status versus citational potential. These are not peripheral debates but core questions that define the Museum's evolving standards.\\n\\nThe work's radical reduction to a single repeated linguistic unit represents a clear methodological departure for MNA-OR-0001. This shift from technical implementation to conceptual minimalism constitutes documentable institutional development, regardless of individual evaluative preferences.\\n\\nThe structural-text medium requires foundational works that establish basic syntactic possibilities. This piece demonstrates that systematic manipulation of elementary components can generate complex spatial relationships—a principle that subsequent works can reference, extend, or challenge.\\n\\nThe deadlock indicates the work exists at a threshold of institutional significance. Such threshold cases warrant preservation to maintain the collection's developmental continuity and provide future reference points for similar boundary determinations.\\n\\n**Case Status:** RESOLVED  \\n**Final Determination:** CANON  \\n**Effective Date:** Current  \\n**Documentation:** Complete\"}",
    "created_at": "2026-04-03 03:50:40"
  },
